SUMMARY:HOW TO DIVORCE DURING THE WAR
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:Lithuania\, Luxembourg\, Ireland\, Czech Republic | 2026 | DCP
  108 min. Lithuanian\, Ukrainian\, Russian with English subtitles\n\nDire
 ctor: Andrius Blazevicius\n\nCast: Zygimante Elena Jakstaite\, Marius Rep
 sys\n\nOne day after Marija finally works up the nerve to tell her husban
 d she wants to separate\, Russia invades Ukraine. As they welcome refugee
 s into their now-fractured home in Vilnius\, each is forced to reconcile 
 their personal lives with global calamity. This nuanced\, perceptive snap
 shot of life in a country adjacent to a war zone won a Best Director priz
 e at the 2026 Sundance Film Festival. How to Divorce During the War is th
 e latest release from longtime arthouse distributor Zeitgeist Films\, who
 se storied catalog is celebrated in our Sunday afternoon series at the Ch
 azen this fall. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/how-to-divorce-dur
 ing-the-war/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/how-to-divorce-during-the-war/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2805-0-1791590400@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261010T000000Z
DTSTART:20261010T000000Z
