SUMMARY:ISHTAR
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1987 | DCP| 107 mins.\n\nDirector: Elaine May\n\nCast: W
 arren Beatty\, Dustin Hoffman\, Isabelle Adjani\n\nHoffman and Beatty are
  inept songwriters who find themselves embroiled in a C.I.A.-engineered s
 py plot in the Middle East. Before this terrific satire on Reagan-era for
 eign policy had been seen by anyone\, audiences had their minds made up f
 or them by the “info-tainment” press corps who relentlessly reported 
 the high production costs and portrayed the gifted May as a filmmaker-out
 -of-control. She sadly hasn’t directed a film since.\n\nhttps://cinema.
 wisc.edu/events/ishtar/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/ishtar/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2806-0-1791676800@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261011T000000Z
DTSTART:20261011T000000Z
DTEND:20261011T014100Z
SUMMARY:WHITE NIGHTS (LE NOTTI BIANCHE)
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:Italy | 1957 | DCP | 101 min. | Italian with English subtitles
 \n\nDirector: Luchino Visconti\n\nCast: Marcello Mastroianni\, Maria Sche
 ll\, Jean Marais\n\nVisconti’s ravishing adaptation of a Dostoevsky sto
 ry stars Mastroianni and Schell as two lonely souls whose chance meeting 
 on a moonlit canal blossoms into a fragile romance haunted by past loves 
 and melancholy longing. Set within a dreamlike\, studio-built city of sha
 dowy streets and shimmering canals\, the film transforms a fleeting encou
 nter into an achingly beautiful meditation on love. This new 4K restorati
 on brings the breathtaking black-and-white imagery of Le notti bianche ba
 ck to the big screen\, allowing cinema viewers to discover one of the gre
 at masterpieces of postwar Italian cinema.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/eve
 nts/white-nights-le-notti-bianche/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/white-nights-le-notti-bianche/
END:VEVENT
