SUMMARY:SENSE AND SENSIBILITY – Free Advance Screening!
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque
DESCRIPTION:USA\, UK | 2026 | DCP | 131 min.\n\nDirector: Georgia Oakley\n
 \nCast: Daisy Edgar-Jones\, Esmé Creed-Miles\, George MacKay\n\nFrom di
 rector Georgia Oakley (Blue Jean\, WFF 2023) comes an irresistible new ta
 ke on Jane Austen’s canonical novel Sense and Sensibility: a charming\,
  witty\, and deeply relatable story of love and sisterhood. This free adv
 ance screening is courtesy Focus Features. Sense and Sensibility opens 
 in theaters October 16.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/sense-and-sensi
 bility/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/sense-and-sensibility/
END:VEVENT
