SUMMARY:BRIGHT VICTORY
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1951 | 35mm | 97 min.\n\nDirector: Mark Robson\n\nCast: 
 Arthur Kennedy\, James Edwards\, Peggy Dow\n\nAfter he gets blinded by a 
 German sniper’s bullet in 1943\, Sergeant Larry Nevins (Kennedy\, in an
  Oscar-nominated lead performance) begins the long and painful road to re
 covery. Landing in a military hospital\, Larry pursues a romance with att
 ending nurse Judy (Dow)\, while his casual racism affects his growing fri
 endship with an African-American soldier\, Joe (Edwards). This powerful\,
  somewhat neglected postwar drama about a veteran’s redemption through 
 courage and love will be screened in an excellent 35mm archival print. Pr
 esented in conjunction with the exhibition Craft/Work: A History of Occup
 ational and Art Therapies\, open in the Ebling Library Historical Reading
  Room from September 8 through December 17.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/ev
 ents/bright-victory/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/bright-victory/
END:VEVENT
