SUMMARY:JOSIE AND THE PUSSYCATS
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 2001 | 35mm | 98 min.\n\nDirector: Harry Elfont\, Debora
 h Kaplan\n\nCast: Rachael Leigh Cook\, Rosario Dawson\, Parker Posey\n\nW
 hen an evil record label implants subliminal messaging in pop music to br
 ainwash the youth\, rock trio Josie and the Pussycats become their unwitt
 ing Trojan Horse. Josie’s buoyant spoof of consumerism gamely extends t
 he gag to the film itself\, which is an unparalleled parody of product pl
 acement. Simultaneously subversive and escapist\, this underrated comedy 
 features a memorable batch of mall-punk cuts by alt-rock ringers like Ada
 m Schlesinger. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/josie-and-the-pussy
 cats/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/josie-and-the-pussycats/
END:VEVENT
