DTSTART:20261114T024500Z
DTEND:20261114T053300Z
SUMMARY:There Will Be Blood (2007) [Open Caption Screening]
LOCATION:The Marquee\, Union South
DESCRIPTION:US | 158 min | R | Dir. Paul Thomas Anderson\n\n"Silver miner 
 Daniel Plainview (Daniel Day-Lewis) leads a hardscrabble life with his so
 n\, H.W. (Dillon Freasier). When he hears about oil oozing from the groun
 d near the Western town of Little Boston\, Daniel takes his son on a miss
 ion to find their fortune. Daniel makes his lucky strike and becomes a se
 lf-made tycoon but\, as his fortune grows\, he deviates into moral bankru
 ptcy." - Rotten Tomatoes\n"The film is above all a consummate work of art
 \, one that transcends the historically fraught context of its making\, a
 nd its pleasures are unapologetically aesthetic. It reveals\, excites\, d
 isturbs\, provokes\, but the window it opens is to human consciousness it
 self."        - Manohla Dargis for New York Times\n \n \n \nWatch 
 the trailer here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FeSLPELpMeM \n \n \n
 For information on available assistive content for WUD Film screenings\, 
 please visit the Assistive Movie Screenings in the Marquee Theater page.
   \nVisit our Informed Moviegoing Resources page for links to resources
  that explore film ratings and content alerts.\nThis event is intended fo
 r UW-Madison students\, faculty\, staff\, Wisconsin Union members and the
 ir guests. Anyone can become a Wisconsin Union member.\n\nhttps://union.w
 isc.edu/events-and-activities/event-calendar/event/wud-film-presents-ther
 e-will-be-blood-2007-open-caption\n\nSource: WUD Film (The Marquee)
URL:https://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activities/event-calendar/event/wud-
 film-presents-there-will-be-blood-2007-open-caption
