BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2820-0-1794704400@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261115T010000Z
DTSTART:20261115T010000Z
DTEND:20261115T040300Z
SUMMARY:RRR
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:India | 2022 | DCP | 183 min. | Telugu with English subtitles\
 n\nDirector: S.S. Rajamouli\n\nCast: N.T. Rama Rao Jr.\, Ram Charan\, Oli
 via Morris\n\nAfter breaking box office records for Telugu cinema with hi
 s epic Baahubali saga\, writer/director S.S. Rajamouli achieved unprecede
 nted global crossover success with the rollicking RRR. Rajamouli’s film
  follows Bheem (Rao) and Raju (Charan)\, fictionalized versions of real-l
 ife revolutionaries—and men emerging from different backgrounds during 
 British colonial rule in 1920s India. Their unlikely friendship leads to 
 a powerful alliance in opposition to the regime in this unrivaled fusion 
 of blockbuster excess\, blood-stained brotherhood\, and musical ecstasy. 
 A word-of-mouth sensation in the U.S. upon its release\, RRR won the Best
  Original Song Oscar for its centerpiece number\, “Naatu Naatu.” (JM)
 \n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/rrr/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/rrr/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2821-0-1794772800@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261115T200000Z
DTSTART:20261115T200000Z
DTEND:20261115T223100Z
SUMMARY:BAAHUBALI: THE BEGINNING
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:India | 2015 | DCP | 151 min. | Telugu with English subtitles\
 n\nDirector: S.S. Rajamouli\n\nCast: Prabhas\, Rana Daggubati\, Anushka S
 hetty\n\nA larger-than-life saga etched with the force of an ancient myth
 \, Rajamouli’s mammoth sword-and-sandals epic changed the trajectory of
  Indian cinema. When a dashing young warrior discovers his royal heritage
 \, he sets out to reclaim the throne from the corrupt regime. Boasting ja
 w-dropping battle sequences\, searing melodrama\, and spectacular filmmak
 ing\, the Baahubali films shattered Indian box-office records. Originally
  released in two parts separated by nearly two years of anticipation (an 
 agonizing wait after The Beginning’s notorious cliffhanger)\, don’t m
 iss this chance to experience the full Baahubali in one glorious binge\, 
 presented with a 20 minute intermission. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/
 events/baahubali-the-beginning/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/baahubali-the-beginning/
END:VEVENT
