SUMMARY:Good Boy (2025) [Polish Film Festival]
LOCATION:The Marquee\, Union South
DESCRIPTION:Poland | 110 min | NR | Dir. Jan Komasa\n \n"A 19-year-old cr
 iminal\, Tommy\, is kidnapped and forced into a rehabilitation process by
  a dysfunctional couple\, Chris and Kathryn\, who try to make him a "good
  boy." Tommy must find a way to escape". -IMDB\n"Simply sublime\, dark\, 
 and unnerving" - BOOM\nWatch the trailer here: https://www.imdb.com/video
 /vi866241305/?ref_=tt_vids_vi_t_2 \n \nThe Madison Polish Film Festival
  is a free annual event organized by the UW-Madison Polish Student Associ
 ation in collaboration with the Department of German\, Nordic\, and Slavi
 c+ and Wisconsin Union Directorate (WUD) Film Committee\, and sponsored b
 y the Lapinski Family Fund\, CREECA\, and the Polish Heritage Club of Mad
 ison.  \n \n \nFor information on available assistive content for WUD 
 Film screenings\, please visit the Assistive Movie Screenings in the Marq
 uee Theater page.  \nVisit our Informed Moviegoing Resources page for l
 inks to resources that explore film ratings and content alerts.\nThis eve
 nt is intended for UW-Madison students\, faculty\, staff\, Wisconsin Unio
 n members and their guests. Anyone can become a Wisconsin Union member.\n
 \nhttps://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activities/event-calendar/event/wud-f
 ilm-presents-good-boy-2025-polish-film-festival\n\nSource: WUD Film (The 
