DESCRIPTION:Poland | 113 min | NR | Dir. Lukasz Palkowski\n \n"Confronted
  with a malevolent interrogator in a Soviet prisoner-of-war camp\, a youn
 g Polish lieutenant fights for his life and the soul of his country."\nWa
 tch the trailer here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OmqnHUr2AkA \n \n
 The Madison Polish Film Festival is a free annual event organized by the 
 UW-Madison Polish Student Association in collaboration with the Departmen
 t of German\, Nordic\, and Slavic+ and Wisconsin Union Directorate (WUD) 
 Film Committee\, and sponsored by the Lapinski Family Fund\, CREECA\, and
  the Polish Heritage Club of Madison.  \n \nFor information on availabl
 e assistive content for WUD Film screenings\, please visit the Assistive 
 Movie Screenings in the Marquee Theater page.  \nVisit our Informed Mov
 iegoing Resources page for links to resources that explore film ratings a
 nd content alerts.\nThis event is intended for UW-Madison students\, facu
 lty\, staff\, Wisconsin Union members and their guests. Anyone can become
  a Wisconsin Union member.\n\nhttps://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activitie
 s/event-calendar/event/wud-film-presents-duelgorky-resort-2026-polish-fil
 m\n\nSource: WUD Film (The Marquee)
