SUMMARY:CHRONOVISOR
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | DCP | 2026 | 100 min. | French\, English\, German\, and 
 Italian with English subtitles\n\nDirector: Kevin Walker\, Jack Auen\n\nC
 ast: Anne-Laure Sellier\n\nIn the 1960s\, an Italian Benedictine monk cla
 imed to have invented a machine that allowed users to see into the past\,
  as though on a TV set. While doing research\, present-day academic Béat
 rice becomes fascinated by this “Chronovisor\,” and plunges headlong 
 into uncovering the truth about this mysterious device. This unusual and 
 beguiling indie perfectly captures the sensation of going down a rabbit h
 ole of dubious arcana. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/chronovisor
 /\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/chronovisor/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2823-0-1795222800@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261121T010000Z
DTSTART:20261121T010000Z
DTEND:20261121T024200Z
SUMMARY:PARAMOUNT ON PARADE
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1930 | 35mm | 102 min.\n\nDirector: Ernst Lubitsch\, Edm
 und Goulding\, Dorothy Arzner and 8 others\n\nCast: Gary Cooper\, Clara B
 ow\, Fredric March\n\nA great burst of pre-code fun\, Paramount on Parade
  was Paramount Pictures’ contribution to the all-star studio musical re
 vue movie cycle of the early talkie years. Featuring 20 individual segmen
 ts from 11 directors\, the movie is literally a showcase for the incredib
 le talents under contract: Gary Cooper\, Clara Bow\, Fredric March\, Maur
 ice Chavalier\, Jean Arthur\, Kay Francis\, Jack Oakie\, William Powell\,
  Fay Wray\, and lots\, lots more stars. Hard to see for many years\, a fe
 w sequences have been lost or partially lost. This 35mm preservation prin
 t courtesy the UCLA Film & Television Archive restores the two-color Tech
 nicolor to several sequences and is the most complete version available. 
 35mm restored print courtesy of the UCLA Film & Television Archive.\n\nht
 tps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/paramount-on-parade/\n\nSource: UW Cinemathe
 que
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/paramount-on-parade/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2824-0-1795309200@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261122T010000Z
DTSTART:20261122T010000Z
DTEND:20261122T030000Z
SUMMARY:MICHAEL MANN’S MANHUNTER: THE FINAL CUT
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1986 | DCP | 120 min.\n\nDirector: Michael Mann\n\nCast:
  William Petersen\, Brian Cox\, Tom Noonan\n\nBefore Jonathan Demme’s T
 he Silence of the Lambs\, writer/director Michael Mann first brought Thom
 as Harris’ popular series of crime novels to the screen with this allur
 ing adaptation of Red Dragon. Retreating to a quiet life with his family 
 after taking down the infamous Hannibal Lecktor (Cox)\, FBI “manhunter
 ” Will Graham (Petersen) returns to work following the emergence of an 
 enigmatic new killer. An extraordinarily stylish modern thriller\, Manhun
 ter is an immersive portrait of Graham’s obsessive pursuit. Mann has de
 clared this new 4K restoration to be the final\, definitive version of hi
 s landmark procedural. (JM)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/michael-man
 ns-manhunter-the-final-cut/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/michael-manns-manhunter-the-final-cut/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2825-0-1795377600@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261122T200000Z
DTSTART:20261122T200000Z
DTEND:20261122T214000Z
SUMMARY:CAREFUL
LOCATION:Chazen Museum of Art\, 750 University Ave\, Madison\, WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:Canada | 1992 | 35mm | 100 min.\n\nDirector: Guy Maddin\n\nCas
 t: Kyle McCullough\, Gosia Dobrowolska\, Paul Cox\n\nHigh in the Alpine v
 illage of Tolzbad\, any loud noise or even strong emotion risks triggerin
 g an avalanche. Consumed by a lifetime of simmering lust and repressed ri
 valries\, one family finally erupts into a feverish torrent of sex and vi
 olence. Designed to evoke the trembling saturation of early two-strip Tec
 hnicolor\, Maddin’s first color feature is an otherworldly pageant of l
 urid artificiality\, which will be in full display on this original relea
 se 35mm print. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/careful/\n\nSource:
  UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/careful/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2826-0-1796346000@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261204T010000Z
DTSTART:20261204T010000Z
DTEND:20261204T023500Z
SUMMARY:BUDDY – Casper Kelly in Person!
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 2026 | DCP | 95 min.\n\nDirector: Casper Kelly\n\nCast: 
 Delaney Quinn\, Cristin Milioti\, Topher Grace\n\nIn the first theatrical
 ly released feature from the inventive mind of writer/director Casper Kel
 ly\, a brave girl and her friends must escape a kids television show. A w
 ild\, unpredictable\, sometimes blood-soaked horror comedy\, Buddy featur
 es stellar work from the cast\, especially young lead Delaney Quinn\, and
  guest appearances from Patton Oswalt\, Michael Shannon\, and Keegan-Mich
 ael Key as the title character. Casper Kelly will join us in person for a
  post-screening discussion!\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/buddy/\n\nS
 ource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/buddy/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2827-0-1796428800@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261205T000000Z
DTSTART:20261205T000000Z
DTEND:20261205T013500Z
SUMMARY:SALESMAN
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1969 | DCP | 95 min.\n\nDirector: David Maysles\, Albert
  Maysles\, Charlotte Zwerin\n\nA landmark American documentary from the t
 eam that later made Grey Gardens and Gimme Shelter\, Salesman marks a hig
 hpoint in 1960s cinema verité. Aging door-to-door Bible salesman Paul Br
 ennan is followed through his struggles with sales quotas and the somber 
 desperation and frustrations of constant travel. As a study of business a
 nd religion\, materialism and spiritualism\, few non-fiction movies speak
  with such sensitivity and subtle beauty.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/even
 ts/salesman/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/salesman/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2828-0-1796436000@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261205T020000Z
DTSTART:20261205T020000Z
DTEND:20261205T031800Z
SUMMARY:ABOUT ENDLESSNESS (OM DET OÄNDLIGA)
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:Sweden | 2019 | DCP | 78 min. | Swedish with English subtitles
 \n\nDirector: Roy Andersson\n\nCast: Martin Serner\, Tatiana Delaunay\, J
 an-Eje Ferling\n\nIn what he has stated will be his final film\, director
  Andersson concludes a quartet of darkly satirical features\, each compos
 ed with a number of vignettes that reveal the foibles and limitations of 
 the human race. Using a locked-down camera and deep focus long takes\, An
 dersson delivers a number of random episodes\, some poignant\, some gag-d
 riven. He also follows a few recurring characters\, such as a priest suff
 ering a crisis of faith\, an older man who feels slighted by an old class
 mate\, and a couple who embrace each other as they float amongst clouds. 
 All of the brief episodes are filmed entirely on brilliantly detailed set
 s at Andersson’s private studio.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/abou
 t-endlessness-om-det-oandliga/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/about-endlessness-om-det-oandliga/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2829-0-1796500800@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261205T200000Z
DTSTART:20261205T200000Z
DTEND:20261205T213100Z
SUMMARY:THE DEVIL AND MISS JONES
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1941 | 35mm | 91 min.\n\nDirector: Sam Wood\n\nCast: Jea
 n Arthur\, Charles Coburn\, Robert Cummings\n\nLooking to bust up union a
 ctivity at his department store\, wealthy tycoon J.P. Merrick (Coburn) go
 es undercover as a shoe salesman in order to identify the organizers. Soo
 n though\, he’s caught up in the lives of his employees\, including uni
 on ringleader Mary Jones (Arthur)\, and Merrick forgets his original purp
 ose…until his two identities collide. This hilarious farce will be show
 n in a restored 35mm preservation print courtesy of the UCLA Film & Telev
 ision Archive.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/the-devil-and-miss-jones
 /\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/the-devil-and-miss-jones/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2830-0-1796508000@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261205T220000Z
DTSTART:20261205T220000Z
DTEND:20261205T234800Z
SUMMARY:UNDER THE SKIN
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:UK\, USA\, Switzerland | 2013 | DCP | 108 min.\n\nDirector: Jo
 nathan Glazer\n\nCast: Scarlett Johansson\, Jeremy McWilliams\, Adam Pear
 son\n\nIn this one-of-a-kind cinematic odyssey from director Jonathan Gla
 zer (The Zone of Interest\, Birth)\, an alien creature takes the form of 
 a woman (Scarlett Johansson) in contemporary Scotland. As this malevolent
  visitor prowls the streets\, various men fall victim to its tantalizing 
 disguise\, yet life as a human soon takes its toll. Guided by a disquieti
 ng musical score from composer Mica Levi\, Glazer’s horrific sci-fi tal
 e features shades of the rigorous formal style employed by Stanley Kubric
 k. Audaciously experimental\, Under the Skin is one of the most acclaimed
  films of the twenty-first century thus far. (JM)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.
 edu/events/under-the-skin/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/under-the-skin/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2831-0-1796518800@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261206T010000Z
DTSTART:20261206T010000Z
DTEND:20261206T023100Z
SUMMARY:ADULT SWIM YULE LOG – Casper Kelly in Person!
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 2022 | DCP | 91 min.\n\nDirector: Casper Kelly\n\nCast: 
 Andrea Laing\, Justin Miles\, Jessica Fontaine\n\nA cozy two-minute yule 
 log video morphs into a disturbing home invasion horror movie that become
 s a supernatural cabin-in-the-woods thriller with a young couple who may 
 be at the mercy of a haunted fireplace! Originally presented on Adult Swi
 m without any announcement or warning\, this wild holiday slay ride found
  immediate appreciation from horror-comedy fans and spawned an equally fu
 n sequel. Yule Log will be preceded by Casper Kelly’s celebrated\, hila
 rious Adult Swim short\, Too Many Cooks (2014\, 11 min.). Casper Kelly wi
 ll join us in person for a post-screening discussion.\n\nhttps://cinema.w
 isc.edu/events/adult-swim-yule-log/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/adult-swim-yule-log/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2832-0-1796580000@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261206T180000Z
DTSTART:20261206T180000Z
DTEND:20261206T195300Z
SUMMARY:THE DREAMLIFE OF ANGELS
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:France | 1998 | 35mm | 113 min. | French with English subtitle
 s\n\nDirector: Erick Zonca\n\nCast: Élodie Bouchez\, Natacha Régnier\, 
 Gregoire Colin\n\nStars Bouchez and Régnier shared the Best Actress priz
 e at the Cannes Film Festival for their raw\, deeply compassionate portra
 its of two young women who develop a friendship on the margins of contemp
 orary France. Refusing easy clichés about youth\, the film follows their
  diverging paths with honesty\, capturing both the exhilaration of possib
 ility and the compromises demanded by adulthood. Screening in a rare 35mm
  print courtesy of the Wisconsin Center for Film & Theater Research\, Dre
 amlife remains one of the great discoveries of 1990s French cinema.\n\nht
 tps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/the-dreamlife-of-angels/\n\nSource: UW Cinem
 atheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/the-dreamlife-of-angels/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2833-0-1796589000@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261206T203000Z
DTSTART:20261206T203000Z
DTEND:20261206T221200Z
SUMMARY:THE PARALLAX VIEW
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1974 | 35mm | 102 min.\n\nDirector: Alan J. Pakula\n\nCa
 st: Warren Beatty\, Paula Prentiss\, Hume Cronyn\n\nBeatty stars as Joe F
 rady\, a journalist obsessed with the assassination of a Kennedy-esque ca
 ndidate. His investigation leads him to the mysterious Parallax Corporati
 on\, which just might be a recruiting organization for assassins. Along w
 ith director Pakula’s All the President’s Men\, this is a bonafide Ho
 llywood classic of political paranoia. 35mm print courtesy Wisconsin Cent
 er for Film & Theater Research.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/the-par
 allax-view/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/the-parallax-view/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2834-0-1797037200@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261212T010000Z
DTSTART:20261212T010000Z
DTEND:20261212T030900Z
SUMMARY:12 MONKEYS
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:USA | 1995 | 35mm | 129 min.\n\nDirector: Terry Gilliam\n\nCas
 t: Bruce Willis\, Brad Pitt\, Madeleine Stowe\n\nWillis stars as a haples
 s “volunteer” from the future\, sent to 20th century Baltimore by the
  post-apocalyptic-powers-that-be to try and figure out who or what trigge
 red a pandemic that killed 99% of the earth’s human population. Directo
 r Gilliam’s Hollywood-blockbuster riff on Chris Marker’s La Jetee tee
 ms with details that bring to life his visions of a dystopian future and 
 the almost-as-dystopian present. 12 Monkeys masterfully combines mordant 
 humor\, surreal lunacy\, big screen sci-fi action set pieces\, and an ach
 ingly vulnerable\, melancholic heart. (BR)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/eve
 nts/12-monkeys/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/12-monkeys/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2835-0-1797105600@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261212T200000Z
DTSTART:20261212T200000Z
DTEND:20261212T230800Z
SUMMARY:FANNY AND ALEXANDER
LOCATION:UW Cinematheque\, 4070 Vilas Hall\, 821 University Ave\, Madison\
 , WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:Sweden | 1982 | 35mm | 188 min. | Swedish with English subtitl
 es\n\nDirector: Ingmar Bergman\n\nCast: Pernilla Allwin\, Bertil Guve\, J
 an Malmsjö\n\nAt the twilight of his illustrious career\, Bergman mined 
 his own childhood memories for this moving family drama told on a grand s
 cale. When the patriarch of the Ekdahls\, a Swedish family of actors in t
 he early twentieth century\, dies suddenly\, the children (Allwin and Guv
 e) must adjust to life under Bishop Edvard (Malmsjö)\, their mother’s 
 cruel new husband. Bergman’s austere mood and signature existential med
 itations here exist in tandem with moments of warmth and joy\, including 
 an extended sequence chronicling the family’s annual Christmas party. A
  35mm print of the film’s theatrical version will be screened. (JM)\n\n
 https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/fanny-and-alexander/\n\nSource: UW Cinemat
 heque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/fanny-and-alexander/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2836-0-1797123600@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261213T010000Z
DTSTART:20261213T010000Z
DTEND:20261213T023000Z
SUMMARY:COMMUNICATION ARTS SHOWCASE – Fall 2026
LOCATION:Marquee Theater at Union South\, 1308 West Dayton St\, Union Sout
 h\n(Second Floor)
DESCRIPTION:USA | 2026 | 90 min.\n\nHighlighting works produced in Communi
 cation Arts Media Production courses at UW Madison\, this program is cura
 ted by the instructors of documentary and narrative production courses an
 d gives new filmmakers the opportunity to present their films on screen f
 or the first time.\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/events/communication-arts-s
 howcase-fall-2026/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/communication-arts-showcase-fall-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cinematheque-2837-0-1797192000@cinema.wisc.edu
DTSTAMP:20261213T200000Z
DTSTART:20261213T200000Z
DTEND:20261213T211600Z
SUMMARY:BLUE
LOCATION:Chazen Museum of Art\, 750 University Ave\, Madison\, WI 53706
DESCRIPTION:UK | 1993 | 35mm | 76 min.\n\nDirector: Derek Jarman\n\nCast: 
 Nigel Terry\, Derek Jarman\, Tilda Swinton\n\nCreated as he was dying of 
 AIDS and losing his sight\, Derek Jarman’s powerful final film famously
  consists of a single image: a screen-filling shade of blue. Blue’s vis
 ual monochrome is contrasted with a richly layered soundscape\, as Jarman
  weaves a poetic account of his life as a gay man in London and impending
  mortality alongside contributions from longtime collaborators like Tilda
  Swinton and music by artists including Brian Eno and Coil. This singular
  cinematic experience will only be enhanced by screening on a 35mm print 
 from the film’s original release. (MK)\n\nhttps://cinema.wisc.edu/event
 s/blue/\n\nSource: UW Cinematheque
URL:https://cinema.wisc.edu/events/blue/
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
